      "description": "Watch Inter Turku vs Istanbul Basaksehir highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 30, 2026. The UEFA Europa Conference League action unfolded on 2026-07-30 as Inter Turku hosted Istanbul Basaksehir in a high-stakes continental encounter. Both sides entered the pitch looking to establish an early foothold, promising a match filled with tactical intrigue and physical competition. Early Breakthrough and Tactical Edge The match ignited early when Ousseynou Ba received a yellow card in just the 10th minute, signaling a tough evening ahead for the visitors. Inter Turku took full advantage of their early momentum in the 18th minute. A brilliant piece of play by Janne-Pekka Laine set up Jasse Tuominen , who clinicaly finished to give the home side the lead. Despite attempts from Istanbul Basaksehir to find an equalizer before the break, the first half concluded with the hosts firmly in control. Second Half Surge and Clinical Finishing Seeking a spark, the visitors made a double substitution at the start of the second half, bringing on Bertug Yildirim and Abbosbek Fayzullayev . However, Inter Turku struck again almost immediately. In the 47th minute, Loic Essomba provided a pinpoint assist for Clinton Jephta , who doubled the lead and sent the home crowd into a frenzy. The goal forced Istanbul Basaksehir into further changes, including the introduction of Berkay Ozcan , as they desperately searched for a way back into the contest. Late Drama and Red Card Tension As the clock ticked down, the intensity rose, leading to several bookings for players like Onur Bulut and Jasse Tuominen . The narrative took a sharp turn in the 88th minute when Janne-Pekka Laine , who had been instrumental earlier, received his second yellow card and was sent off. Faced with a nervous finish and six minutes of added time, the ten-man Inter Turku defense remained resolute, thwarting every late attempt by the Turkish side to secure a hard-earned victory."
